  "compatibility_proof": "For each destructive skill old unrounded polynomial is convex; derivative with respect to tail k >= .192*base. Anchor A differs from its raw value by less than 10. Checked 192*base-30*A>10000, hence old_raw(k)>new_raw(k) for all k>=1. Monotone ceiling preserves old_price>=new_price. Both schedules are >= A, so every mixed history lies inside prefix+count*A and prefix+count*old_last. Bounds remain deliberately conservative, not a reconstruction of exact transactions.",
